---
description: Tests and quality rules
globs:
  - "tests/**/*.php"
  - "phpunit.xml*"
  - "phpstan.neon*"
  - ".php-cs-fixer.dist.php"
  - "rector.php"
alwaysApply: false
---

When changing behavior, prefer adding or updating the nearest relevant test (`tests/Unit/<Namespace>` mirrors `src/`; kernel boot tests live in `tests/Integration`).

Prefer:
- one focused test
- minimal fixture changes
- preserving the existing testing style (PHPUnit attributes such as `#[CoversClass]`, no docblock annotations)
- obvious placeholders for credentials in fixtures (`REDACTED-TEST`, `demo-token`)

Quality gates (run through Docker):
- `make test`, `make coverage-check` (100% PHP line coverage), `make phpstan` (level 8, `ignoreErrors: []`)
- `make cs-check`, `make rector-dry`, `make igor`
- `make release-check` before a release

Do not introduce new testing frameworks unless explicitly requested.
Do not rewrite unrelated tests.
Do not lower the coverage gate or add PHPStan ignores to make a run pass.
